cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using this metadata."
title: "AnomaliRadar: state-aware, empirically calibrated anomaly detection on MetroPT-3"
abstract: >-
  AnomaliRadar is a reproducible research-engineering release for anomaly
  detection on the MetroPT-3 air-production compressor. It composes causal
  context-aware value scoring (Score A), confirmed-state persistence scoring
  (Score B), empirical Mondrian calibration with explicit back-off and refusal,
  a calibration-only alarm-budget solver, OR fusion, and a 30-minute debounce.
  The release includes a deterministic experiment runner, frozen artefacts,
  F1-F9 falsification audit, a test suite and a read-only Streamlit viewer.
  On the primary 1 alarm/observed-day budget the OR method detects 2 of 4
  labelled events with 1 false alarm on the four event folds; the unlabelled
  tail realizes 0.5609 alarms/day. The result is a CONDITIONAL GO with explicit
  small-sample and calibration limitations.
